<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Morija</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1833</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Morija is a village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maseru">Maseru</a> district, Lesotho, founded in 1833 as the first station of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> Evangelical Missionary Society, whose missionaries <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moshoeshoe-i">Moshoeshoe I</a> invited into his kingdom. It became a centre of Christian education and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> in Sesotho, and is home to the Morija Museum and Archives.</p></div>
